{"task_id": "HumanEval/6", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef _calculate_max_nesting(group: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the deepest level of nesting for a single group of parentheses.\n    Handles malformed parentheses by not allowing current_nesting to go below 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    max_nesting = 0\n    current_nesting = 0\n    for char in group:\n        if char == '(':\n            current_nesting += 1\n            max_nesting = max(max_nesting, current_nesting)\n        elif char == ')':\n            current_nesting -= 1\n            # Ensure current_nesting doesn't go negative for malformed strings.\n            current_nesting = max(0, current_nesting)\n    return max_nesting\ndef parse_nested_parens(paren_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Analyzes a string of space-separated parenthesis groups, calculating the deepest nesting level for each.\n    For example, '(()())' has a maximum of two nesting levels.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not paren_string.strip():\n        return []\n\n    groups = paren_string.split(' ')\n    results = []\n    for group in groups:\n        # Strip whitespace from individual groups, accounting for multiple spaces.\n        results.append(_calculate_max_nesting(group.strip()))\n    return results"}
