{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\ndef median(l: list) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    Handles empty lists, non-numeric elements, and calculates median for odd/even lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FR5: Raise ValueError if the input list is empty.\n    if not l:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n    \n    # FR6: Raise TypeError if the input list contains non-numeric elements.\n    if not all(isinstance(x, (int, float)) for x in l):\n        raise TypeError(\"List must contain only numeric elements (int or float).\")\n\n    # FR1.2: Sort the list.\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    # Determine if the list has an odd or even number of elements (FR1.3).\n    if n % 2 == 1:  # Odd number of elements (FR2, BR1)\n        # FR1.4: If odd, return the middle element.\n        mid_idx = n // 2\n        return sorted_l[mid_idx]\n    else:  # Even number of elements (FR3, BR2)\n        # FR1.5: If even, return the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid_right_idx = n // 2\n        mid_left_idx = mid_right_idx - 1\n        # FR4: The average calculation produces a float naturally.\n        return (sorted_l[mid_left_idx] + sorted_l[mid_right_idx]) / 2.0"}
