{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "import math\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the largest prime factor of a given composite integer `n`.\n    Input `n` must be an integer greater than 1 and not prime itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be greater than 1.\")\n\n    def is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if a number is prime.\"\"\"\n        if num <= 1: return False\n        if num <= 3: return True\n        if num % 2 == 0 or num % 3 == 0: return False\n        i = 5\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0 or num % (i + 2) == 0: return False\n            i += 6\n        return True\n\n    if is_prime(n):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must not be a prime number.\")\n\n    largest_factor = 1\n    temp_n = n\n\n    while temp_n % 2 == 0:\n        largest_factor = 2\n        temp_n //= 2\n\n    f = 3\n    while f * f <= temp_n:\n        while temp_n % f == 0:\n            largest_factor = f\n            temp_n //= f\n        f += 2\n\n    if temp_n > 1:\n        largest_factor = temp_n\n\n    return largest_factor"}
