{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "class InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"\n    Custom exception for signaling invalid input parameters.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\ndef fib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 1, 1\n    # Iteratively calculate Fibonacci numbers starting from the 3rd.\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
