{"task_id": "HumanEval/87", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\ndef get_row(lst: List[List[int]], x: int) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds all occurrences of an integer x in a nested list and returns their\n    (row, column) coordinates, sorted by row ascending and then by column descending.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_coordinates: List[Tuple[int, int]] = []\n\n    for r_idx, row in enumerate(lst):\n        for c_idx, item in enumerate(row):\n            if item == x:\n                found_coordinates.append((r_idx, c_idx))\n\n    # Sort primarily by row in ascending order, secondarily by column in descending order.\n    found_coordinates.sort(key=lambda coord: (coord[0], -coord[1]))\n\n    return found_coordinates"}
