{"task_id": "HumanEval/89", "solution": "def encrypt(s):\n    \"\"\"Encrypts a string using a Caesar cipher with a fixed rotation. \n    Alphabetic characters are shifted by 4 positions, preserving case; other characters remain unchanged.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    SHIFT_AMOUNT = 4\n    encrypted_chars = []\n\n    for char in s:\n        if 'a' <= char <= 'z':\n            start = ord('a')\n            shifted_char_code = start + (ord(char) - start + SHIFT_AMOUNT) % 26\n            encrypted_chars.append(chr(shifted_char_code))\n        elif 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            start = ord('A')\n            shifted_char_code = start + (ord(char) - start + SHIFT_AMOUNT) % 26\n            encrypted_chars.append(chr(shifted_char_code))\n        else:\n            encrypted_chars.append(char)\n            \n    return \"\".join(encrypted_chars)"}
