{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "import math\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the closest integer to a numerical string, rounding away from zero for X.5 values.\n    Handles string parsing and applies the specified rounding logic.\n    \"\"\"\n    number = float(value)\n    floor_num = math.floor(number)\n    ceil_num = math.ceil(number)\n\n    if number - floor_num == 0.5:\n        # Equidistant (X.5), round away from zero.\n        # For positive numbers (e.g., 14.5), round up. For negative numbers (e.g., -14.5), round down.\n        if number > 0:\n            return int(ceil_num)\n        else:\n            return int(floor_num)\n    elif number - floor_num < 0.5:\n        # Round down to the lower integer.\n        return int(floor_num)\n    else: # number - floor_num > 0.5\n        # Round up to the higher integer.\n        return int(ceil_num)"}
