{"task_id": "HumanEval/106", "solution": "def f(n):\n    \"\"\"Generates a list of `n` elements based on specific mathematical rules for each 1-based index `i`.\n    If `i` is even, its value is `i!`; if `i` is odd, its value is the sum from 1 to `i`.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_factorial(num: int) -> int:\n        # Calculates the factorial of a given non-negative number.\n        if num == 0:\n            return 1\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(1, num + 1):\n            res *= i\n        return res\n\n    def _calculate_sum_up_to(num: int) -> int:\n        # Calculates the sum of integers from 1 up to a given non-negative number.\n        return (num * (num + 1)) // 2\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index\n            result.append(_calculate_factorial(i))\n        else:  # Odd index\n            result.append(_calculate_sum_up_to(i))\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/106", "solution": "def _factorial(k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the factorial of a non-negative integer k.\n    Returns 1 for k=0; raises ValueError for k < 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Factorial is not defined for negative numbers.\")\n    if k == 0:\n        return 1\n    res = 1\n    for i in range(1, k + 1):\n        res *= i\n    return res\ndef _sum_up_to(k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of integers from 1 up to k using Gauss's formula.\n    Raises ValueError for k < 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Sum up to k is not defined for k < 1.\")\n    return k * (k + 1) // 2\ndef f(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Implement the function f that takes n as a parameter,\n    returning a list of size n based on index parity (1-based).\n    Element i is factorial(i) if even, or sum_up_to(i) if odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n\n    result_list = []\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if i % 2 == 0:  # Even index\n            result_list.append(_factorial(i))\n        else:  # Odd index\n            result_list.append(_sum_up_to(i))\n    return result_list"}
